From 6a7442847901d307a801c6521e05bd0175dc7cbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jraphaelsst <joaoraphaelsst@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 08:49:51 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(seed/cors): derive allow_origin_regex from
 PRODUCT_URL_PATTERN for SSO-bridge
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every new product's SSO was breaking because core's CORS allowlist had no
knowledge of `PRODUCT_URL_PATTERN`—the slim prod container can only emit
origins from explicit `PRODUCT_URL_<SLUG>` env vars, so a new product
(e.g. orbity.noctusai.com) was invisible to CORS until someone hand-added
a per-product env var and recreated core.

This commit wires `allow_origin_regex` into the seed's CORSMiddleware so
the SSO-bridge shape covers any first-party subdomain by construction:

- `cors_registry.derive_cors_origin_regex(pattern)`: builds an anchored
  regex from `PRODUCT_URL_PATTERN` when the slug placeholder is in the
  authority (subdomain-style). Returns None for path-style patterns and
  when no pattern is set (dev no-op). Sentinel-swap + re.escape ensures
  the literal `.` is escaped to `\.` and slug classes land cleanly.
- `BaseAppSettings.cors_origin_regex`: property that is non-None only for
  the `@registry:all` (SSO-bridge) shape; None for all other modes.
- `app_factory.configure_app`: passes `allow_origin_regex=getattr(settings,
  "cors_origin_regex", None)` to CORSMiddleware (getattr for back-compat).
- 33 new tests across cors_registry + app_factory: match/no-match for every
  documented case, literal-dot anchoring, path-style guard, slug_underscored
  variant, settings property isolation.
- Backstop test (`test_allow_origin_regex_wired_for_registry_all_...`)
  inspects the mounted middleware stack to assert the seam is wired — chosen
  over a full keeper because the seam is a single `getattr` call, and the
  test directly exercises the exact CORSMiddleware kwargs at configure_app
  time. Severity surfaced as medium in the test docstring.

Derived regex for `https://{slug}.noctusai.com`:
  `^https://[a-z0-9](?:[a-z0-9\-]*[a-z0-9])?\.noctusai\.com$`

Lenses: backend-engineer

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
